RATIONALE: All four technical reviewers (novelty_killer, systems_reviewer, evaluation_prosecutor, theory_skeptic) voted RED with convergent, independently-derived objections. The product_realist voted YELLOW, acknowledging the mechanism is mathematically sound but flagging the same novelty risk and operational limitations. No RED is unrebutted by evidence from the packet.

The fatal convergence is on the STRAWMAN BASELINE problem: the claim's entire architecture rests on the premise that "document-level near-dedup is the standard practice" for contamination detection. This is empirically false — GPT-3 (2020) uses 13-gram overlap, PaLM (2022) uses 8-gram ≥70% containment, and every contamination survey confirms passage/n-gram is the standard method. Document-level MinHash-LSH (Lee et al. 2021) is a CORPUS DEDUPLICATION tool, not a contamination detector. Measuring that a corpus-dedup tool detects contamination worse than a contamination-detection tool is a category error, not a discovery.

The ALGEBRAIC TAUTOLOGY objection is independently fatal: Jaccard(item, doc) ≈ span_ratio for disjoint vocab is closed-form set arithmetic. The paper itself derives Jaccard≈43/490≈0.09 and then "measures" exactly that value. Confirming textbook math on synthetic data with distinct vocabularies is not an empirical contribution.

The MISSING CONTAINMENT BASELINE is the evaluation_prosecutor's killer experiment: Containment = |A∩B|/|B| yields 1.0 for any fully embedded item, trivially closing the "gap." Its omission means the claim shows only that one specific metric (union-normalized Jaccard) fails — not that "document-level granularity" is fundamentally blind. This is a weaker, analytically predictable result.

The product_realist's YELLOW correctly notes the mechanism is real (Jaccard union normalization DOES dilute short spans) but this is the Lee et al. 2021 motivation for ExactSubstr, not a new finding. The one genuinely novel empirical result — the precision boundary at span_thresh~0.95 under partial-quote confound — is a useful calibration knob but is (a) not what the claim foregrounds, (b) tested only against synthetic confounds, and (c) insufficient to constitute a "quantified granularity gap" contribution when the gap itself is algebraic.

The orchestrator's contingency guidance is triggered: this IS the "already-known-folklore" case (n-gram checks find more than dedup) without a novel quantified contribution beyond confirming textbook arithmetic. The genuinely unmeasured question (real-corpus paraphrase distribution of contamination, which decides whether the verbatim-only gap matters at scale) is exactly the part not done, and even if done, would face the strawman objection that real contamination pipelines already use passage-level methods. Converge PROJ-0013; do not deep-mine this area. <cite>Packet PRIOR-ART CAVEAT (admitting GPT-3/PaLM are passage-level); RESULTS.md "union normalization … 43/490 ≈ 0.09" (confirming closed-form prediction); Lee et al. 2021 arXiv:2107.06499 (NearDup vs ExactSubstr); Brown et al. 2020 arXiv:2005.14165 (GPT-3 13-gram); Chowdhery et al. 2022 arXiv:2204.02311 (PaLM 8-gram ≥70%); Yang et al. 2023 arXiv:2311.04850 (paraphrase fragility); evaluation_prosecutor KILLER_EXPERIMENT (containment baseline); theory_skeptic ASSUMPTIONS_UNTESTED (containment would catch trivially); novelty_killer FATAL_COLLISIONS (≥2 source verification on all axes).</cite>
